       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. CUSTTBL.
      *****************************************************************
      * ACCUMULATES CUSTOMER BALANCES INTO AN OCCURS TABLE. THE        *
      * SUBSCRIPT WS-BAL-IDX IS A POSITION IN THAT TABLE, NOT A PLACE  *
      * THE VALUE LANDS - WIDENING CUST_BALANCE MUST GROW              *
      * WS-BAL-ENTRY AND LEAVE THE INDEX ALONE. THE INDEX IS NUMERIC,  *
      * LIKE THE VALUE, WHICH IS WHY IT USED TO INHERIT THE EXTRA      *
      * DIGITS AND BE REPORTED AS NEEDING TO GROW.                     *
      *****************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
           EXEC SQL INCLUDE CUSTOMER END-EXEC.
       01  WS-BAL-IDX               PIC S9(4)       COMP.
       01  WS-BAL-TABLE.
           05  WS-BAL-ENTRY         PIC S9(9)V99    COMP-3
                                    OCCURS 100 TIMES.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       0000-MAIN.
           MOVE 1 TO WS-BAL-IDX
           EXEC SQL
               SELECT CUST_BALANCE
                 INTO :CUST-BALANCE
                 FROM CUSTOMER
                WHERE CUST_ID = :CUST-ID
           END-EXEC
           MOVE CUST-BALANCE TO WS-BAL-ENTRY(WS-BAL-IDX)
           GOBACK.
